This project focuses on predicting diabetes risk using patient clinical data with a Machine Learning classification model built using **Support Vector Machine (SVM)** and deployed through an interactive **Streamlit web application**.

🔹 **Project Workflow**
✔ Data preprocessing using **NumPy** and **Pandas**
✔ Feature scaling with **StandardScaler**
✔ Dataset splitting using **train_test_split**
✔ Model training using **Linear SVM Classifier** from Scikit-learn
✔ Model evaluation using **Accuracy Score**
✔ Model & scaler serialization using **Pickle**
✔ Interactive deployment using **Streamlit**
✔ Visualization using **Plotly Gauge Charts**

📊 **Features Used for Prediction**
• Pregnancies
• Glucose Level
• Blood Pressure
• Skin Thickness
• Insulin
• BMI
• Diabetes Pedigree Function
• Age

🧠 **Machine Learning Details**
The model was trained using a **linear kernel SVM classifier** after standardizing the dataset to improve performance and prediction accuracy.

The dataset was split into training and testing sets with stratified sampling to maintain balanced class distribution. The trained model was then saved as:
• `diabetes_model.pkl`
• `scaler.pkl`

💻 **Application Features**
✨ Modern responsive UI with custom CSS
✨ Real-time diabetes risk prediction
✨ Probability confidence gauge
✨ Feature health range analysis
✨ Risk indicators with visual feedback
✨ Interactive Plotly dashboard
✨ Streamlit-powered deployment

📈 The system predicts whether a patient has a high or low diabetes risk and displays:
✔ Diabetes probability
✔ Confidence percentage
✔ Risk gauge visualization
✔ Out-of-range health indicators

🛠 **Tech Stack**
Python | Scikit-learn | Streamlit | Plotly | NumPy | Pandas | Pickle

